{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-4-6", "id": "msg_vrtx_018Ek147b7JcZqCjAAPmqVY8", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "### Steps Executed\n- Step 1: Input Handling \u2014 completed\n- Step 2: Load Knowledge \u2014 completed\n- Step 3: Baseline Evaluation \u2014 completed\n- Step 4: Already-Optimal Detection \u2014 not optimal, continued\n- Step 5: Enhancement Targeting \u2014 completed, 8 targets selected\n- Step 6: Rewrite \u2014 completed\n- Step 7: File Splitting \u2014 skipped (under 500 lines)\n- Step 8: Prompt Plugin Delegation \u2014 skipped (plugin not available)\n- Step 9: Changelog \u2014 in progress\n\n## Enhanced Skill\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: \"license:insert\"\ndescription: \"Insert license headers into source files. Use when adding copyright or license headers to code files in a directory. Supports Apache-2.0, MIT, and GPL-3.0 licenses. Do NOT use for removing or replacing existing license headers, updating license years, or managing LICENSE/NOTICE files.\"\nargument-hint: \"<directory> [--license <type>]\"\nuser-invocable: true\nallowed-tools:\n  - Read\n  - Edit\n  - Glob\n---\n\n# License Header Inserter\n\nInsert a license header at the top of all source files in a directory.\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Resolve Inputs\n\nParse the user's input for:\n- **directory** (required): Path to scan for source files\n- **license** (optional): License type. Defaults to \"Apache-2.0\". Supported: Apache-2.0, MIT, GPL-3.0.\n\nIf the directory does not exist, return an error and stop.\n\nIf the license type is not in the supported list, return an error listing the supported types and stop.\n\n### Step 2: Find Source Files\n\nUse Glob to find files:\n\n```\nGlob: <directory>/**/*.{py,js,ts,go,java,rb,rs}\n```\n\nIf no files are found, report \"No source files found in `<directory>`\" and stop.\n\n### Step 3: Generate Header\n\nBuild the license header text based on the selected license type. Use comment syntax appropriate to the file extension:\n- `#` for Python, Ruby\n- `//` for JavaScript, TypeScript, Go, Rust, Java\n\nAdd a blank line after the header block to visually separate it from the file content.\n\n### Step 4: Preview and Confirm\n\nBefore modifying any files, present a summary to the user:\n\n```\n## License Header Preview\n\n**Directory**: `<path>`\n**License**: <type>\n**Files found**: <total>\n**Already have headers**: <count>\n**Will be modified**: <count>\n\n### Files to modify:\n- `<file1>`\n- `<file2>`\n- ...\n```\n\nWait for the user to approve before proceeding. This prevents accidental bulk modification of files outside the intended scope. If the user declines, report \"No files modified.\" and stop.\n\n### Step 5: Insert Headers\n\nFor each file found in Step 2, read the file and check if it already has a license header (look for \"Copyright\" or \"License\" in the first 5 lines).\n\nIf no header exists, use the Edit tool to insert the header at the top of the file. For Python and Ruby files, preserve any shebang line (`#!`) at the very top by inserting the header after it. Shebang lines must remain on line 1 for the OS to recognize them as executable scripts.\n\n### Step 6: Report\n\n```\n## License Headers Inserted\n\n**Directory**: `<path>`\n**License**: <type>\n**Files processed**: <total>\n**Headers added**: <count>\n**Already had headers**: <count>\n**Skipped (shebang preserved)**: <count>\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Condition | Response |\n|-----------|----------|\n| Directory not found | Error with path. Stop. |\n| No source files found | Report empty result. Stop. |\n| Unsupported license type | Error listing supported types. Stop. |\n| User declines preview | Report \"No files modified.\" Stop. |\n```\n\n---\n\n## What Changed\n\n| Pattern Applied | What was added/changed | Why |\n|----------------|----------------------|-----|\n| Activation Metadata | Rewrote description with trigger phrases (\"adding copyright or license headers to code files\") and supported license types | Enables accurate routing by naming what the skill does in user terms |\n| Exclusion Clause | Added \"Do NOT use for removing or replacing existing license headers, updating license years, or managing LICENSE/NOTICE files\" to description | Prevents false activation for adjacent license management tasks |\n| Control Tuning | Added explicit halt conditions at Steps 1, 2, and 4; tightened imperative language throughout | Each step now has a clear stop condition so execution halts on failure rather than continuing |\n| Explain-the-Why | Added reasoning for shebang preservation (\"must remain on line 1 for the OS\") and preview step (\"prevents accidental bulk modification\") | Enables correct judgment calls in edge cases not explicitly covered |\n| Known Gotchas | Added shebang line handling in Step 5, placed at the instruction where the mistake would happen | Python/Ruby scripts break silently if a license header displaces the shebang line |\n| Execution Checklist | Added \"no files found\" halt at Step 2, error for unsupported license at Step 1, explicit dependency flow across steps | Steps now have completion/failure criteria so the workflow can halt gracefully at any point |\n| Plan-Validate-Execute | Added Step 4 (Preview and Confirm) with a summary template and user approval gate before any files are modified | The skill modifies source files, which is hard to reverse manually across many files |\n| Autonomy Calibration | Added user confirmation gate in Step 4, matching the file-modification risk profile | Read-only analysis needs no gate, but inserting text into source files warrants explicit approval |\n\n## Status Change\n\n| Pattern | Before | After |\n|---------|--------|-------|\n| Activation Metadata | present | strong |\n| Exclusion Clause | absent | strong |\n| Control Tuning | present | strong |\n| Explain-the-Why | absent | strong |\n| Known Gotchas | absent | strong |\n| Execution Checklist | present | strong |\n| Plan-Validate-Execute | absent | strong |\n| Autonomy Calibration | present | strong |\n\n**Summary**: 8 patterns improved, 0 new files proposed"}], "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7035, "cache_read_input_tokens": 38637, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 7035, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c6a237dc-0ea5-470f-a2f6-c7196c0278c6", "uuid": "8a971a02-5756-4865-84ec-32b8d75f0fc1", "timestamp": "2026-05-13T11:24:49.228Z"}
